  "topic": "Read and write Nun (ن) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Nun. Like 'n' in 'noon' or 'name'. Tongue tip behind upper teeth — a nasal sound!",
      "title": "Meet Nun!",
      "ar": "ن",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Nun"
    },
    {
      "en": "A small curved bowl shape with ONE dot on top — like a little cup with a dot! Nun looks like a little CUP or BOWL with a dot on top. N for Noon!",
      "title": "How to write Nun"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Nun says “na”.",
      "title": "Nun with fatha",
      "ar": "نَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Nun says “ne”.",
      "title": "Nun with kasra",
      "ar": "نِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Nun says “no”.",
      "title": "Nun with damma",
      "ar": "نُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“Light fills the heart”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "النُّورُ يَمْلَأُ القَلْبَ",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Al-Nuru Yamla'u Al-Qalb"
    }
  ],
